    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#mandinka">Mandinka</a> state in today's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#guinea-bissau">Guinea-Bissau</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#senegambia">Senegambia</a> that began as a western province of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#mali-empire">Mali Empire</a>.</li><li>Ruled by the nyancho warrior aristocracy, it grew rich by selling war captives into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#atlantic-slave-trade">Atlantic slave trade</a> for guns and goods.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#fula">Fula</a> forces from Futa Jallon destroyed its capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#kansala">Kansala</a> in 1867, and the region later fell to European colonial rule.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>At the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#kansala">Kansala</a> in 1867, the mansaba Janke Waali had the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#gunpowder">gunpowder</a> stores ignited, destroying the city, its defenders and many of the attackers.</p></aside>
    </section>

